Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JSC m68k: take the task hooks off at exit

Patch 0033 puts a switch and a launch hook (tc_Switch, tc_Launch, with
TF_SWITCH and TF_LAUNCH) on every task that runs JavaScript, and never
took them off. A program started from a Shell runs on the Shell's own
process, which lives on after the program has gone and its code is freed.
Exec's task switcher went on calling the two hooks in that freed memory
each time the Shell's task was switched; when the next program was loaded
over it the machine hung (a jump into half-loaded code in supervisor mode
with interrupts off, then address 0).

jsc_m68k_detach_threads() takes the hooks and the two flags off every
task that still has ours, inside Disable(), and forgets the tasks. A
destructor calls it when the program ends; a program may also call it
itself before it ends.

Seen with the test viewer run twice in a row from one Shell, the first
run on a page with scripts (17 November 2026). The browser started from
a Shell that stays open had the same fault.

Team 2
---
  Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp
@@ -499,6 +499,33 @@
     task->tc_Flags |= TF_SWITCH | TF_LAUNCH;
     Enable();
 }
+
+// At exit the hooks come off again. The main thread is often not ours to
+// end: a program started from a Shell runs on the Shell's own process,
+// which lives on after the program's code is freed. Left on, exec's task
+// switcher went on calling the hooks in that freed memory, and the next
+// program loaded there hung the machine (17 November 2026: a second run
+// of the viewer straight after a first that had run a page's scripts).
+extern "C" void jsc_m68k_detach_threads()
+{
+    Disable();
+    for (auto& thread : m68kThreads) {
+        struct Task* task = thread.task;
+        if (task && m68kTaskExists(task)
+            && task->tc_Launch == reinterpret_cast<decltype(task->tc_Launch)>(jsc_m68k_task_launch)) {
+            task->tc_Flags &= ~(TF_SWITCH | TF_LAUNCH);
+            task->tc_Switch = nullptr;
+            task->tc_Launch = nullptr;
+        }
+        thread.task = nullptr;
+    }
+    Enable();
+}
+
+__attribute__((destructor)) static void detachM68KThreadsAtExit()
+{
+    jsc_m68k_detach_threads();
+}
 #endif
 
 JSValue CLoop::execute(OpcodeID entryOpcodeID, void* executableAddress, VM* vm, ProtoCallFrame* protoCallFrame, bool isInitializationPass)
